{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"8ce9852dc1a160d1","name":"card_event_defeat_in_detail","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BloodIron/events/card_event_defeat_in_detail","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DEFEAT IN DETAIL","text":"Your units get: \"Gets +1+1 when it damages the enemy HQ.\"","flavorText":"The Battle of Savo Island, also known as the First Battle of the Solomon Sea, was fought on August 8-9, 1942. It was a significant naval battle during WWII and part of the larger Guadalcanal Campaign in the Pacific Theater. It was the first major engagement between Allied and Japanese naval forces following the US invasion of Guadalcanal. A Japanese cruiser force, under Vice Admiral Gunichi Mikawa, launched a surprise night attack on Allied ships patrolling off Savo Island, near Guadalcanal. The Allies, primarily American and Australian forces, were unprepared for the assault. Mikawa’s fleet sank four Allied heavy cruisers (three American, one Australian) and heavily damaged another, marking one of the worst defeats in US Navy history. The Japanese achieved a decisive tactical victory, inflicting heavy losses on the Allies. However, the Japanese failed to press their advantage by not attacking the transport ships supporting the Guadalcanal invasion. This allowed the US forces to maintain a foothold on the island, which became a critical turning point in the Pacific War. The battle highlighted the effectiveness of Japanese night-fighting tactics, which allowed the Japanese Navy to defeat Allied naval forces in detail, suffering only light damage in return.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Rare","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_defeat_in_detail","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_defeat_in_detail_title","SourceString":"DEFEAT IN DETAIL","LocalizedString":"DEFEAT IN DETAIL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_defeat_in_detail_text","SourceString":"Your units get: \"Gets +1+1 when it damages the enemy HQ.\"","LocalizedString":"Your units get: \"Gets +1+1 when it damages the enemy HQ.\""},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_defeat_in_detail_history","SourceString":"The Battle of Savo Island, also known as the First Battle of the Solomon Sea, was fought on August 8-9, 1942. It was a significant naval battle during WWII and part of the larger Guadalcanal Campaign in the Pacific Theater. It was the first major engagement between Allied and Japanese naval forces following the US invasion of Guadalcanal. A Japanese cruiser force, under Vice Admiral Gunichi Mikawa, launched a surprise night attack on Allied ships patrolling off Savo Island, near Guadalcanal. The Allies, primarily American and Australian forces, were unprepared for the assault. Mikawa’s fleet sank four Allied heavy cruisers (three American, one Australian) and heavily damaged another, marking one of the worst defeats in US Navy history. The Japanese achieved a decisive tactical victory, inflicting heavy losses on the Allies. However, the Japanese failed to press their advantage by not attacking the transport ships supporting the Guadalcanal invasion. This allowed the US forces to maintain a foothold on the island, which became a critical turning point in the Pacific War. The battle highlighted the effectiveness of Japanese night-fighting tactics, which allowed the Japanese Navy to defeat Allied naval forces in detail, suffering only light damage in return.","LocalizedString":"The Battle of Savo Island, also known as the First Battle of the Solomon Sea, was fought on August 8-9, 1942. It was a significant naval battle during WWII and part of the larger Guadalcanal Campaign in the Pacific Theater. It was the first major engagement between Allied and Japanese naval forces following the US invasion of Guadalcanal. A Japanese cruiser force, under Vice Admiral Gunichi Mikawa, launched a surprise night attack on Allied ships patrolling off Savo Island, near Guadalcanal. The Allies, primarily American and Australian forces, were unprepared for the assault. Mikawa’s fleet sank four Allied heavy cruisers (three American, one Australian) and heavily damaged another, marking one of the worst defeats in US Navy history. The Japanese achieved a decisive tactical victory, inflicting heavy losses on the Allies. However, the Japanese failed to press their advantage by not attacking the transport ships supporting the Guadalcanal invasion. This allowed the US forces to maintain a foothold on the island, which became a critical turning point in the Pacific War. The battle highlighted the effectiveness of Japanese night-fighting tactics, which allowed the Japanese Navy to defeat Allied naval forces in detail, suffering only light damage in return."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDealDamage"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Waves/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Taiko_Hits_1.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Winter_2024/t_defeat_in_detail.t_defeat_in_detail","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Japanese WWII Poster","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DEFEAT_IN_DETAIL.DEFEAT_IN_DETAIL","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":369.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_defeat_in_detail_photo","SourceString":"American cruiser USS Quincy illuminated in searchlights while on fire and sinking from Japanese torpedoes during the Battle of Savo Island, 1942.","LocalizedString":"American cruiser USS Quincy illuminated in searchlights while on fire and sinking from Japanese torpedoes during the Battle of Savo Island, 1942."},"isDraw":true,"isDefenseBuff":true},"variables":[{"name":"tempCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_event_defeat_in_detail","owner":"card_event_defeat_in_detail_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsValid_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_targetCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_GetAllCardsOnBoard_cards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Get_Item","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Array_Length_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_IsUnit_isIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Less_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_EqualEqual_ByteByte_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_BooleanAND_ReturnValue","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_CustomAbilityAdd_qqq","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_ChangeAttack_qqq","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_ChangeDefense_qqq","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_cardDealingDamage","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_toCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_damage","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_isCombatDamage","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_CounterDamage","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"K2Node_Event_isRedirected","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_HasCustomAbilityFromCard_doesIt","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"